#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:8
msgid "Interfaces (topics, services, actions)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:10
msgid ""
"Interfaces in ROS define how nodes exchange data. This article explains the "
"different types of ROS interface and the differences between them. With this "
"information, you'll be able to select the right interfaces for your purposes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:14
msgid "**Area: ROS-framework | Content-type: concept | Experience: beginner**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:18
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:29
msgid "Summary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:31
msgid ""
"ROS nodes typically communicate through the following three types of "
"interfaces:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:33
msgid "Topics: For continuous data streams."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:34
msgid ""
"Services: For synchronous request/response interactions (short tasks which "
"happen immediately)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:35
msgid ""
"Actions: For long-running tasks with feedback (tasks that may take some time "
"to complete)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:37
msgid ""
"For consistent communication, each interface uses definitions provided in ``."
"msg``, ``.srv``, or ``.action`` files."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:39
msgid ":doc:`Learn more about nodes <About-Nodes>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:42
msgid "Topics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:44
msgid ""
"The topic interface is meant for continuous data streams, for example, "
"streaming sensor data or the status of your robot. Topic definitions are "
"stored in ``.msg`` files. Topics implement a publish/subscribe pattern. A "
"node publishes data to a topic, and other nodes subscribe to receive that "
"data. This interface type has the following main characteristics:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:50
msgid "Asynchronous, one-way communication"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:51
msgid "Multiple publishers and subscribers can share the same topic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:60
msgid ""
"Topic keys identify individual publishers on a topic so nodes and tools can "
"distinguish where messages come from. Each topic key makes it easier to "
"track data sources when several publishers share the same topic."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:64
msgid "Topic statistics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:65
msgid ""
"Topic statistics are built-in measurements that help you understand how "
"messages behave when a subscription receives them. When enabled, they "
"automatically track two things:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:0
msgid "Message age"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:68
msgid "How old a message is when it arrives, based on its timestamp."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:0
msgid "Message period"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:69
msgid "The time between incoming messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:71
msgid ""
"For both message age and period, ROS calculates the average, minimum, "
"maximum, standard deviation, and the number of samples, using a moving "
"window that updates every time a new message arrives. These calculations run "
"in constant time and memory using the dedicated utilities. When you enable "
"topic statistics for a subscription, ROS publishes the collected data at "
"regular intervals as a ``MetricsMessage`` on a statistics topic. This gives "
"you a clear view of timing patterns, delays, and irregularities, making it "
"easier to assess system performance or diagnose problems related to the "
"message flow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:78
msgid ""
"The default interval is 1 second. The default statistics topic is ``/"
"statistics``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:81
msgid ""
":doc:`Learn how to enable topic statistics </Tutorials/Advanced/Topic-"
"Statistics-Tutorial/Topic-Statistics-Tutorial>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:84
msgid "Services"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:86
msgid ""
"The service interface is meant for synchronous request/response "
"interactions, for example, when you want to send a query requesting the "
"configuration of a specific robot. Service definitions are stored in ``."
"srv`` files. Services implement a request/response pattern. A client sends a "
"request, and a server replies with a response. This interface type has the "
"following main characteristics:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:92
msgid "Synchronous communication"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:93
msgid ""
"Ideal for short-lived operations that require confirmation, or provide a "
"result in response to a request"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:104
msgid "Actions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:106
msgid ""
"The action interface is meant for long-running tasks with feedback, for "
"example, moving a robot to a specific position, or asking the robot to "
"perform a complex motion. Action definitions are stored in ``.action`` "
"files. Actions allow clients to send goals, receive feedback during the "
"execution, cancel if needed, and return a result if available. This "
"interface type has the following main characteristics:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:111
msgid "Asynchronous, with feedback and result"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Concepts/Basic/Interfaces-Topics-Services-Actions.rst:112
msgid "Suitable for operations that take time"
msgstr ""

